            <ArticleTitle>Steps in the management of low back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>109-24; discussion 124, 130</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Steps for facilitating management include: 1) identification and referral of patients with a nonmechanical cause of pain, such as cancer or an aortic aneurysm; 2) matching the analgesic agent and the mobilization schedule to the patient's condition and pace of recovery; 3) referring patients whose condition may require surgery; 4) and caring for the remaining patients who have chronic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
